; A value leaving the region it was allocated in - AX3059, the two
; shapes a scope check can refuse without region TYPES.
;
; `(region r body)` reclaims, when `body` ends, everything `body`
; allocated. Anything still pointing into that memory afterwards points
; at bytes the next allocation hands out again, and reading it does
; not fail loudly: it answers the NEXT value's bytes.
; `scripts/check-region-scope.sh` measures exactly that, with the
; refusal below ablated - `hello world` stored into `out` from inside a
; region reads back as the string built after it.
;
;   (a) the region's own VALUE, when its type is not a scalar. The
;       lowering hands the value past the reset by value, and only a
;       scalar survives that; a `String` is a 24-byte descriptor over a
;       second block. Anchored at the BODY, which is what has to change.
;   (b) a `set` inside the region on a binding bound OUTSIDE it, when
;       the stored value is not a scalar. Anchored at the store.
;   (c) the same through a field path: `(set b.s v)` is a store into
;       `b`, and `b` was bound outside.
;
; The three SILENT shapes below them are the half that must not move:
; a scalar leaves a region by value, a scalar store to an outer
; counter is what a region inside a loop needs, and a store to a
; binding made INSIDE the region dies with it. Each is written with
; the reference the refused shape carries, so a refusal that keyed on
; "a `strConcat` appears in the body" would draw three rows too many.
;
; Every row is AX3059 with the one slug `region-escape`: a code has one
; slug, and the message says which shape it was.
(import IO)

(import Str)

(struct Box
  (mut s : String))

(:: main Int)

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (main)
  (let (
    (mut out "")
    (mut n 0)
    (b (Box ""))
  )
    {
      ; --- (a) the value ---
      (region r (strConcat "a" "b"))
      ; --- (b) a store to an outer binding ---
      (region s
        {
          (set out (strConcat "a" "b"))
          0
        })
      ; --- (c) a store into an outer struct's field ---
      (region t
        {
          (set b.s (strConcat "c" "d"))
          0
        })
      ; --- silent: a scalar leaves ---
      (println (region u (strLen (strConcat "a" "b"))))
      ; --- silent: a scalar store to an outer counter ---
      (region v (set n (+ n (strLen (strConcat "a" "b")))))
      ; --- silent: a store to a binding made inside ---
      (region w
        (let ((mut inner ""))
          {
            (set inner (strConcat "x" "y"))
            (strLen inner)
          }))
      (println n)
      (println (strLen out))
      0
    }
  )
)
